{"id": "1.2-00005", "case_id": "github_alexforencich_axil_adapter_direct_v1", "parent_id": null, "source": "github/alexforencich/verilog-axi", "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Agent task and scoring</h2><div class='card'><table><tbody><tr><th style='width:175px'>Input task</th><td class='path'>Project specification, interfaces, and permitted public assets</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Agent context</th><td class='path'>Direct agent workspace: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00005&amp;file_q=public%2F'>public/</a> (5 files)</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Expected output</th><td class='path'>Required RTL: rtl/axil_adapter.v, rtl/axil_adapter_wr.v, rtl/axil_adapter_rd.v. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00005&amp;file=public%2Foutput_contract.json'>Open full output contract</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Hidden reference</th><td class='path'>3 RTL files under private/reference/; <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00005&amp;file=private%2Freference%2Frtl%2Faxil_adapter.v'>open first reference file</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Private score</th><td class='path'>Passed verification testpoints divided by total testpoints, using testbenches or formal verification<br><strong>4 verification testpoints:</strong> cocotb_test_axil_adapter, myhdl_test_axil_adapter_16_32, myhdl_test_axil_adapter_32_16, myhdl_test_axil_adapter_32_32. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00005&amp;file=private%2Fscoring.json'>Open private scoring contract</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Case-stored agent instruction</h2><div class='card'><p class='muted'>These are case-stored instructions. A launcher may add framing or execution limits; its saved trajectory is the exact runtime record.</p><details><summary>public/instruction.md · <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00005&amp;file=public%2Finstruction.md'>Open raw</a></summary><pre># AXI-Lite width-adapter project\nImplement every file and module in output_contract.json. Read the unchanged original README and declaration-only interfaces. Only the selected independent design and its complete RTL closure are requested; unrelated repository components and FPGA board designs are separate designs. Rising clk edges and synchronous active-high rst apply throughout. Assert reset initially for several clocks. Transfer ready/valid signals only on a rising edge with both asserted; preserve data while stalled. Internal state encoding and buffering may differ, but externally visible data, completion and error semantics must match. Private scoring uses one complete usable upstream testbench per point; vectors inside a bench are not additional points. The original source is withheld. Curator clarifications below supplement the original documents and take precedence where explicitly correcting ambiguity.\n\nImplement axil_adapter integrating axil_adapter_rd and axil_adapter_wr. The README wrapper names for this module accidentally omit the l; the required actual children are axil_adapter_rd/wr, as the declaration-only contract shows.\n\n- Convert between S_DATA_WIDTH and M_DATA_WIDTH while preserving byte-addressed memory semantics, protection bits and ready/valid backpressure. Eight-bit bytes, power-of-two word byte counts, common address width, and an integral power-of-two width ratio are required. Read and write paths operate independently. Reset clears transaction/response valids synchronously.\n- Equal widths: relay transactions and responses with handshaking. S narrower than M: perform one wide downstream access, position data/strobes in the destination lane selected by the address, and select that lane for the upstream read data. Repeated narrow writes must preserve adjacent lanes using strobes.\n- S wider than M: split a source word into successive narrow accesses in increasing byte-address order, starting at the addressed narrow segment. Collect read segments into the corresponding source word lanes; divide write data/strobes correspondingly. Return one upstream response only after all required segments complete. The source master issues legal word accesses; AXI-Lite has no burst-length signal.\n- Propagate downstream response codes. For narrowed multiple-access transfers, initialize aggregate response to OKAY and retain a non-OKAY downstream response (a later non-OKAY response replaces the previous error). Do not treat a partial transfer as a completed source request.\n- Preserve all four usable upstream benches: cocotb plus MyHDL 16-&gt;32, 32-&gt;16 and 32-&gt;32. These width configurations are verification points of one adapter design, not four project cases. Golden qualification covers normal read/write byte preservation and stalls; not every downstream-error race is independently covered.\n\nOriginal-document scope: the unchanged README identifies this project, its split read/write architecture and public capabilities. The detailed handshake/reset/corner-case descriptions above are labeled curator clarifications reviewed against the pinned RTL before any model evaluation. Initial blocks containing only parameter diagnostic calls are removed in normalized reference; all functional storage/control remains unchanged.\n\nSimulation I/O, delays, force/release, final blocks and external includes are forbidden. Constant elaboration functions ($clog2, $unsigned, $signed, $bits) and synthesizable storage initialization are permitted. Save all RTL under the exact required paths; only those files are collected.\n</pre></details></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/8d4c0bbbff8b715cd756e1c1298b540c182df44ed9b299a3c2addbbbe6ae00c1.txt", "size": 13531, "binary": false, "section": "Other: case.json"}, {"name": "environment/runtime.json", "url": "assets/9379564162e044e31602be3094e35aa3e6db065b6118a330f0b79ef42b775c9b.txt", "size": 5316, "binary": false, "section": "Other: environment"}, {"name": "private/direct_adapter.json", "url": "assets/d04371de773b6ccc610753be1d848d13a86a7c53267223d7c97fd0ea99697c4f.txt", "size": 539, 